{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["The reason for <b>“And Moses declared the appointed seasons of YHWH to the children of Israel”</b> is that the preceding sections are warnings to Aaron and his sons, and Moses would speak them to Aaron and to his sons, and sometimes he would also mention after them the children of Israel, as he said at the end of the section on blemishes (Leviticus 21:24): “And Moses spoke to Aaron and to his sons and to all the children of Israel,” for even though he was commanded only “Speak to Aaron, any man of your seed” (ibid. v. 17), he wished to warn the court of Israel concerning this as well. Or perhaps the reason is because a person conceals his blemishes, and the priest does not wish to be disqualified from the service, for it is shame and humiliation to him, and therefore the court is warned in this matter. But here it says that he declared the appointed seasons of YHWH to the children of Israel — to all of them equally; he did not single out the sons of Aaron among them. The reason is that the warning applies equally to all, for the essence of the sections is about resting on the Sabbaths and on the appointed seasons and proclaiming them a holy convocation, and there is no mention of offerings in them except only the omer offering (Leviticus 23:12–13) and the two loaves (vv. 18–20), which are the cause. And in the section concerning the essence of the offerings of Yom HaKippurim, he said (Leviticus 16:2): “Speak to Aaron your brother.”\nAnd our Sages interpreted it (Sifra, Emor ch. 17:12): “And Moses declared the appointed seasons of YHWH to the children of Israel” — this teaches that Moses would say to Israel the laws of Pesach at Pesach, and the laws of Atzeret at Atzeret, and the laws of the Chag at the Chag; in whichever language one hears it, in that language he would say to them all the sections.\nOnkelos (Onkelos on Leviticus 23:44) also intended this, as he said: “And Moses set forth the order of the appointed seasons of YHWH and instructed them.” And it appears that his intention was to hint that he taught them the order of the appointed seasons with the rules of intercalation that were transmitted to him orally at Sinai, and this is alluded to in “which you shall proclaim them, holy convocations” (above v. 4), and he taught them orally the entire order received in the sod of intercalation:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "I have translated סוד העיבור literally as 'the sod of intercalation,' preserving the cryptic kabbalistic/esoteric register without explication."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:59:04.558784288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}